REGEDIT4

; Tell Media Foundation that a .webm can be opened, by mapping it to the
; GStreamer byte-stream handler that CrossOver already registers as a COM
; server ("Generic Decodebin Byte Stream Handler").
;
; This is the whole of what winevideo contributes to DYNASTY WARRIORS: ORIGINS
; on CrossOver Preview. Preview already ships the pieces that do the work --
; libgstmatroska for the container and libgstapplemedia, whose VideoToolbox
; path decodes VP9 in hardware -- but without this mapping Media Foundation
; refuses to open the file at all, so the decoder never gets a chance.
;
; .mkv and .msd are the other two winevideo adds; only .webm matters here.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows Media Foundation\ByteStreamHandlers\.webm]
"{317df618-5e5a-468a-9f15-d827a9a08162}"="GStreamer Byte Stream Handler"
